WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  relief for the family of ahmad arbury  hand in hand they walked down the  courtroom steps after his killers were  given life in prison i knew that today  would come  when  when it would come  i didn't know but i know today would  finally come amen  on the 23rd of february 2020 ahmad  arbury a black american had gone out for  a run in a predominantly white  neighborhood in the u.s state of georgia  and never came home  instead he was targeted by these three  men who have now been sentenced for his  murder  a judge said that mr aubry was pursued  in pickup trucks for five minutes before  being cornered and shot by father and  son greg and travis mcmichael and their  neighbor william bryan who claimed they  were attempting a citizen's arrest on a  suspected burglar  he was killed  because individuals here in this  courtroom  took the law into their own hands  but the case has again raised questions  about racial justice in the southern  united states  mr aubry's family lawyers described the  incident as a modern-day lynching and in  response to the jury's verdict in  november president biden said we must  recommit ourselves to building a future  of unity and shared strength where no  one fears violence because of the colour  of their skin  the men waved their right to address the  court at the hearing but their lawyers  say they plan to appeal the convictions  katie barnfield sky news

